    <!-- The lever catalogue: one phrase per position, read by the pre-game screen and by
         the notification a rule fires. Each is a full sentence with a verb, and it states a
         state and never an event, because the same phrase serves both places: "3 lives are
         left", never "you lose a life".

         Two things it never does. It does not name the app or the AI: what speaks is a
         character, and any voice beyond that belongs to the staging phrase, which the author
         of a scene writes on the patch. And it does not address the learner unless the
         sentence genuinely needs a subject: a screen listing twenty of these would be a
         wall of "you". -->
